  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The problem states that Jane’s account **pays 2% annual interest** and compounds once at the end of each year.\n\nTherefore, the annual interest rate is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Jane has saved $4 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Changing Jane’s weekly savings from \\$5 to \\$4 does not change the account’s interest rate. The account still pays:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Jane will continue saving the same amount each week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The amount Jane saves and how often she deposits it do not affect the account’s stated interest rate. The account pays **2% annual interest**, compounded once per year.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Jane's allowance savings are measured in dollars per week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves \\(\\$4\\) per week, but this is her **saving rate**, not the account’s interest rate. The account still offers an annual interest rate of\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much money will Jane have saved from her allowance after one full year? Also, here's some more context: Jane saves money for 52 weeks in a year. This calculation ignores any interest earned in the account.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves \\(\\$4\\) each week for \\(52\\) weeks:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 52 = 208\n\\]\n\nIgnoring interest, Jane will have saved\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$208}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Her weekly saving rate is constant throughout the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Jane saves a constant \\(\\$4\\) per week for \\(52\\) weeks:\n\n\\[\n\\$4 \\times 52 = \\$208\n\\]\n\nIgnoring interest, she will have saved\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$208}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many more weeks will Jane need to save to have a total savings of $60? By the way, Jane wants to have saved a total of $60.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane has already saved:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times \\$4=\\$32\n\\]\n\nShe needs:\n\n\\[\n\\$60-\\$32=\\$28\n\\]\n\nAt \\(\\$4\\) per week, the additional number of weeks is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$28}{\\$4\\text{/week}}=7\\text{ weeks}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ more weeks}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
